@page
@model MossHarper.Pages.ServicesModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Our services";
}

<section class="v17-services-page v17-section" aria-labelledby="services-page-title">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="v17-section-intro"><div><p class="v17-eyebrow">Our services</p><h1 id="services-page-title">Where we can help.</h1><span class="v17-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span></div><div><p>Every property challenge has its own circumstances. We offer focused advice and practical support across the areas below, from independent assessment to carefully planned improvement.</p><strong>Select a service to explore the ways Moss Harper may be able to assist.</strong></div></div>
        <div class="v17-accordion-list">
            <details id="managing-agent" class="v17-service-item" open><summary><span class="v17-service-number">01</span><span><strong>Independent Managing Agent &amp; Operational Reviews</strong><small>Independent scrutiny of management performance, service delivery and accountability.</small></span><span class="v17-service-toggle" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="v17-service-body"><div><p>An effective review looks beyond individual complaints to establish whether the management structure, resources, contracts and reporting arrangements are fit for purpose. Moss Harper can evaluate existing arrangements, identify underlying causes of underperformance and recommend practical changes.</p></div><div><h2>Illustrative areas of support</h2><ul><li>Managing agent performance and service-delivery reviews</li><li>On-site and central staffing structures, responsibilities and reporting</li><li>Contract management, procurement, service standards and value for money</li><li>Operational improvement plans and support with management transitions</li></ul></div></div></details>

            <details id="service-charge" class="v17-service-item" open><summary><span class="v17-service-number">02</span><span><strong>Service Charge Reviews &amp; Financial Performance</strong><small>Establishing whether expenditure is appropriate, justified and reflected in the services delivered.</small></span><span class="v17-service-toggle" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><p class="v17-service-quote">The objective is not simply to reduce expenditure, but to establish whether costs are appropriate, justified and delivering the intended services.</p><div class="v17-service-body"><div><p>Complex service-charge budgets can be difficult to interrogate. We help clients review budgets, cost allocation, procurement arrangements and financial controls, with particular attention to the relationship between expenditure and actual service delivery.</p></div><div><h2>Illustrative areas of support</h2><ul><li>Budget scrutiny, cost allocation and expenditure reviews</li><li>Review of contracts, procurement, staffing and utility costs</li><li>Value-for-money and service-delivery assessments</li><li>Clear, evidence-based recommendations for improvement</li></ul></div></div></details>

            <details id="transformation" class="v17-service-item" open><summary><span class="v17-service-number">03</span><span><strong>Strategic &amp; Operational Transformation</strong><small>Restructuring teams, improving operating models and strengthening performance through practical change.</small></span><span class="v17-service-toggle" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="v17-service-body"><div><p>Operational transformation must work in practice, not simply on paper. Drawing on experience of restructuring central and site-based teams, establishing technical functions and introducing digital platforms, we support businesses seeking clearer accountability and more resilient service delivery. This can include interim senior leadership advice, development handover and estate mobilisation, and operational due diligence for acquisitions.</p></div><div><h2>Illustrative areas of support</h2><ul><li>Operating-model reviews and organisational restructuring</li><li>Site-based and central team design, management reporting and accountability</li><li>Technology and process improvement, including resident-facing platforms</li><li>Interim or part-time executive support, management transitions and change oversight</li><li>Developer handover, estate mobilisation and operational due diligence for investors</li></ul></div></div></details>

            <details id="building-safety" class="v17-service-item" open><summary><span class="v17-service-number">04</span><span><strong>Building Safety &amp; Regulatory Compliance</strong><small>Operational support for higher-risk buildings, building-safety governance and regulator engagement.</small></span><span class="v17-service-toggle" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="v17-service-body"><div><p>Building safety requires clear responsibility, reliable information and effective coordination across management and specialist disciplines. We assist with the operational and governance challenges of the regime and help clients engage appropriately qualified professionals when technical judgements or statutory certifications are required.</p></div><div><h2>Illustrative areas of support</h2><ul><li>Accountable-person arrangements and building-safety management reviews</li><li>Building Safety Regulator engagement and Building Assessment Certificate process support</li><li>Safety Case Report coordination, resident-engagement arrangements and information governance</li><li>External-wall remediation programme coordination and operational risk review</li></ul></div></div></details>

            <details id="heat-networks" class="v17-service-item" open><summary><span class="v17-service-number">05</span><span><strong>Heat Networks &amp; Utility Management</strong><small>Clarifying performance, costs and responsibilities as heat networks enter Ofgem regulation.</small></span><span class="v17-service-toggle" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="v17-service-body"><div><p>Heat networks sit where engineering, operating contracts, billing and resident experience meet. Ofgem became the sector regulator in January 2026, and relevant existing heat networks must be registered by 26 January 2027. Moss Harper helps owners, managing agents and RMCs review operational and commercial arrangements, clarify responsibilities and assess readiness, coordinating specialist technical or regulatory input where required.</p></div><div><h2>Illustrative areas of support</h2><ul><li>Operational readiness reviews covering Ofgem registration and consumer-protection requirements</li><li>Operator and maintenance arrangements, contracts and responsibilities</li><li>Heat-network expenditure, billing structures and service-charge implications</li><li>Performance concerns and efficiency reviews with appropriate technical specialists</li><li>Resident communication and practical improvement plans</li></ul></div></div></details>

            <details id="resident-engagement" class="v17-service-item" open><summary><span class="v17-service-number">06</span><span><strong>Resident Engagement &amp; Communication</strong><small>Helping property businesses communicate clearly, respond consistently and rebuild confidence.</small></span><span class="v17-service-toggle" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="v17-service-body"><div><p>When residents do not know what is happening, why decisions have been made or when matters will be resolved, uncertainty can quickly undermine trust. Effective engagement means providing timely, accurate information, listening to concerns and making responsibilities and progress visible. It is not about defending every decision; it is about demonstrating accountability.</p></div><div><h2>Illustrative areas of support</h2><ul><li>Resident communication and stakeholder-engagement reviews</li><li>Meeting preparation, consultation and communication around major works or building safety</li><li>Complaint-handling, escalation and recurring-issue analysis</li><li>Digital platforms for recording, tracking and communicating progress</li></ul></div></div></details>

            <details id="dispute-resolution" class="v17-service-item" open><summary><span class="v17-service-number">07</span><span><strong>Early Dispute Assessment, Resolution &amp; Tribunal Support</strong><small>Assessing the facts and the respective positions early, before disputes escalate unnecessarily.</small></span><span class="v17-service-toggle" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="v17-service-body"><div><p>Moss Harper can assess the underlying management, financial and contractual issues, help clients understand the strengths and weaknesses of their position and explore early resolution. Our role is defined before an instruction begins: in a given matter we may provide a neutral assessment or act for one party, including with case preparation or permitted representation before the First-tier Tribunal (Property Chamber), but we will not act as both a neutral expert and an advocate in the same matter.</p></div><div><h2>Illustrative areas of support</h2><ul><li>Independent issue assessments for freeholders, managing agents and leaseholders</li><li>Service-charge disputes, factual investigation and early resolution discussions</li><li>Document review, evidence collation and case preparation</li><li>First-tier Tribunal support and permitted representation, with legal specialists involved where needed</li></ul></div></div></details>
        </div>
        <div class="v17-services-foot"><p>Assignments are tailored to the issue and may involve bringing in appropriately qualified external specialists where required.</p><a class="v17-text-link" asp-page="/Contact" asp-fragment="contact">Discuss your challenge <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="v17-protect v17-section" aria-labelledby="protect-title"><div class="container v17-protect-grid"><div><p class="v17-eyebrow v17-eyebrow-gold">Protecting what matters</p><h2 id="protect-title">Small problems can become reputational ones quickly.</h2><span class="v17-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span></div><div><p>Weak management, unresolved resident concerns and poor communication can expose property businesses to more than additional costs. They can undermine confidence and cause lasting reputational harm.</p><p>In an environment where concerns can spread rapidly through resident networks and social media, our focus is early assessment, constructive intervention and meaningful corrective action.</p><p class="v17-protect-quote">A credible response is more valuable than a defensive one.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="v17-closing"><div class="container"><p class="v17-eyebrow v17-eyebrow-gold">Start a conversation</p><h2>What challenge are you trying to resolve?</h2><a class="v17-button v17-button-gold" asp-page="/Contact" asp-fragment="contact">Discuss your challenge <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></section>
